==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹʌfəl/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-ruffle.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌfəl}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any [[gathered]] or [[curled]] strip of fabric added as [[trim]] or [[decoration]].
#: ''She loved the dress with the lace '''ruffle''' at the hem.
#* {{RQ:Chrsty Atbgrfy|II|4}}
#*: Mind you, clothes were clothes in those days. [&hellip;]&nbsp; Frills, '''ruffles''', flounces, lace, complicated seams and gores: not only did they sweep the ground and have to be held up in one hand elegantly as you walked along, but they had little capes or coats or feather boas.
# [[disturbance|Disturbance]]; [[agitation]]; [[commotion]].
#: ''to put the mind in a '''ruffle'''''
# {{lb|en|military}} A low, vibrating [[beat]] of a [[drum]], quieter than a [[roll]]; a [[ruff]].
#: {{rfquotek|en|H. L. Scott}}
# {{lb|en|zoology}} The connected series of large [[egg]] [[capsule]]s, or [[ootheca]]e, of several [[species]] of [[American]] [[marine]] [[gastropod]]s of the [[genus]] ''[[Fulgur]]''.

